  "content": {
    "id": "p33-task21-25-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Determine whether the following pairs of lines are parallel, perpendicular, or neither.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-task21-25-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$y=4x+2$ and $y=4x-5$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Parallel.",
          "worked": "$m_1=4$ and $m_2=4$.\n\nThe gradients are equal and the $y$-intercepts are different, so the lines are parallel.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-task21-25-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$y=-\\frac{1}{3}x+7$ and $y=3x-1$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Perpendicular.",
          "worked": "$m_1=-\\frac{1}{3}$ and $m_2=3$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}m_1m_2 &= \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)(3)\\\\m_1m_2 &= -1\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe lines are perpendicular.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-task21-25-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$6x+5y-1=0$ and $5x+6y+1=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Neither parallel nor perpendicular.\n\nThe gradients are $-\\frac{6}{5}$ and $-\\frac{5}{6}$: they are unequal and their product is $1$.",
          "worked": "The first line is $y=-\\frac{6}{5}x+\\frac{1}{5}$, giving $m_1=-\\frac{6}{5}$.\n\nThe second line is $y=-\\frac{5}{6}x-\\frac{1}{6}$, giving $m_2=-\\frac{5}{6}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}m_1m_2 &= \\left(-\\frac{6}{5}\\right)\\left(-\\frac{5}{6}\\right)\\\\m_1m_2 &= 1\\end{align*}$$\n\nSince $m_1\\ne m_2$ and $m_1m_2\\ne-1$, the lines are neither parallel nor perpendicular.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-task21-25-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$2x-3y+6=0$ and $3x+2y-8=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Perpendicular.",
          "worked": "The first line is $y=\\frac{2}{3}x+2$, giving $m_1=\\frac{2}{3}$.\n\nThe second line is $y=-\\frac{3}{2}x+4$, giving $m_2=-\\frac{3}{2}$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}m_1m_2 &= \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\left(-\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\\\m_1m_2 &= -1\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe lines are perpendicular.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-task21-25-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "$3x+2y+1=0$ and $6x+4y+5=0$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Parallel.",
          "worked": "The first line is $y=-\\frac{3}{2}x-\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nThe second line is $y=-\\frac{3}{2}x-\\frac{5}{4}$.\n\nBoth gradients are $-\\frac{3}{2}$ and the $y$-intercepts are different, so the lines are parallel.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      }
    ]
  },
